  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000123343,
      "SummaryText": "The 212 Nuway Packing Dr facility in Forest City, NC follows the requirements of the OSHA Process Management Program, 29 CFR 1910.119 and the EPA's Risk Management program, 40 CFR Part 68 in that it addresses the following requirements; Employee Participation, Process Safety Information, Process Hazard Analysis, Operating Procedures, Training, Contractor Qualifications, Pre-start Up Safety Review, Mechanical Integrity, Hot Work, Management of Change, Incident Investigation, Emergency Planning, and Compliance Audits. There are no trade secrets.\n\nThe only chemical that meets the threshold requirements is Anhydrous Ammonia of which there is 15,000 lbs. The ammonia is used in the ice manufacturing process. \n\nAs part of the ammonia refrigeration system, there are several release prevention measures that include, ammonia alarms, sensors, high pressure cutouts for compressors, emergency control panel for system shutdown and manual/automatic emergency ventilation activation.\n\nFor emergency planning purposes, the facility operates as defensive action only and relies on the Forest City fire department and Rutherford County emergency management to provide emergency response. An Emergency Action Plan is in place.\n\nThere have been no ammonia accidents within the last 5 years.\n\nThe facility has engaged HCG Associates, LLC, a consulting firm that specializes in ammonia refrigeration system compliance, to assist in developing robust safety programs to prevent and mitigate any accidental releases of anhydrous ammonia."
    }
  ]
